# A plan under development is never published, and this is what makes that true
# rather than merely intended: `git add -A` during implementation would
# otherwise stage it, and a plan is exactly the document that might name an
# unpatched vulnerability, an auth-bypass specific, a customer or an embargoed
# launch.
#
# A plan reaches `main` only when David asks for it, deliberately, with the
# disclosure check in front of it.
#
# COMMITTED RATHER THAN LEFT TO THE SCRIPT. `ensurePlansIgnored` writes this
# file on demand in any repository that runs a planning exchange, which is what
# protects a fresh consumer. In THIS repository the directory is used by hand
# too -- a plan copied in before any exchange has run is a plan nothing is
# ignoring yet, which is a gap reached during the loop's own live validation on
# 2026-09-18. Committing it makes the protection exist before the script rather
# than because of it. The pattern matches what the script looks for, so a later
# run finds it and appends nothing.
PLAN_*.md
